The dataset consisted of five EEG sets, A through E, each containing 100 single-channel EEG signals of 23.6 seconds duration. Signals were sampled at 173.61 Hz after 12-bit analog-to-digital conversion, band-pass filtered at 0.53 to 40 Hz, and recorded using a 128-channel amplifier system with an average common reference. Set A represented healthy eyes-open activity, Set B healthy eyes-closed activity, Set C seizure-free hippocampal activity from the opposite hemisphere, Set D seizure-free activity from the epileptogenic zone, and Set E seizure activity. K-means was configured with K=4 after empirical evaluation and used random partition initialization. The classifiers were implemented in WEKA with default settings, with LIBSVM version 3.2 used for SVM, and calculations were carried out in MATLAB R2015b. The experimental setting was a two-class classification task within a benchmark database, not a cross-patient, multi-patient, or invariant-risk-minimization study.
