In the provided excerpt, the quantitative result is an ablation showing that predicting a fixed randomly initialized target network yields 18.8% top-1 accuracy on linear ImageNet evaluation, compared with 1.4% for the randomly initialized network alone. The excerpt also states that BYOL did not converge to collapsed equilibria in experiments, but it does not report the final BYOL ImageNet accuracy or comparisons to baselines in the supplied text.
[context]
Experiments were on ImageNet ILSVRC-2012 training data with linear evaluation. The base architecture was ResNet-50 with 2048-dimensional pooled features; projection and predictor MLPs used 4096 hidden units and 256 output units. Augmentations included random crop/resize, horizontal flip, color distortion, optional grayscale, Gaussian blur, and solarization. The paper excerpt does not specify batch size, learning-rate schedule, or GPU/CPU hardware, so it does not directly validate the proposed setup of 40 EEG clips per batch, cosine annealing, RTX 3090, and Xeon Gold 6248R.
